<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<UserControl
    x:Class="Winhance.UI.Features.Common.Controls.FeatureOutcomeBanner"
    xmlns="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml/presentation"
    xmlns:x="http://schemas.microsoft.com/winfx/2006/xaml"
    xmlns:fluentIcons="using:FluentIcons.WinUI"
    xmlns:local="using:Winhance.UI.Features.Common.Controls">

    <!--
    Reports, on a feature's overview card, that Winhance could not determine the state of some settings
    inside it. Attaches to the BOTTOM of the card so it is unmistakably about that feature: the parent
    StackPanel spaces its children by 8, so -9 closes that gap and overlaps the border by 1, and the top
    corners are squared while the bottom stay rounded - the same join the settings cards use.

    This REPLACED per-outcome info-badge pills. A detection outcome is a fault, not a badge: badges say
    where a value sits relative to our advice, which is optional detail and reasonably hidden behind
    View > InfoBadges. Hiding "1 setting is saved in the wrong format" behind that same toggle was
    backwards - so this is deliberately NOT gated by it.

    SEVERITY IS ALWAYS INFORMATIONAL, and the per-outcome colour lives on the ITEMS instead. An earlier
    version set the bar's severity to the worst outcome present, which backfired: a feature holding one
    wrong-format and one unrecognized setting turned the whole bar amber, and the eye then went looking
    for amber only - the blue one effectively disappeared. A neutral bar carrying one coloured chip per
    kind tells you exactly what to hunt for once you click in, which is the only job this banner has.
    -->
    <Border Visibility="{x:Bind BannerVisibility, Mode=OneWay}" Margin="0,-9,0,0">
        <local:QuietInfoBar
            IsOpen="{x:Bind IsBannerOpen, Mode=OneWay}"
            Severity="Informational"
            Message="{x:Bind BannerMessage, Mode=OneWay}"
            IsClosable="False"
            IsTabStop="True"
            UseSystemFocusVisuals="True"
            CornerRadius="0,0,4,4">
            <!-- One chip per outcome KIND present, each with the same icon those settings carry on
                 their own controls, so a colour means one thing everywhere in the app. -->
            <ItemsControl ItemsSource="{x:Bind Fragments, Mode=OneWay}" Margin="0,0,0,4">
                <ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                    <ItemsPanelTemplate>
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="16"/>
                    </ItemsPanelTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemsPanel>
                <ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
                    <DataTemplate x:DataType="local:FeatureOutcomeFragment">
                        <StackPanel Orientation="Horizontal" Spacing="6" VerticalAlignment="Center">
                            <fluentIcons:FluentIcon Icon="{x:Bind Icon}" IconVariant="Color"
                                                    FontSize="15" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                            <TextBlock Text="{x:Bind Text}" VerticalAlignment="Center"/>
                        </StackPanel>
                    </DataTemplate>
                </ItemsControl.ItemTemplate>
            </ItemsControl>
        </local:QuietInfoBar>
    </Border>
</UserControl>
